--- body ---
## Context

The current `inspect()` path verifies native pack identity and versions but
never checks its text content. A well-formed empty pack therefore follows the
same `current` path as a pack containing text. Ticket 0744 consumes the
corrected classification; SPEC.md §5.2.7 owns its meaning and display.

The earlier external pdftotext sample concerned only initial pages and was
not a complete native-pack content inspection. It motivates investigation,
but does not prove a document has no text layer, diagnose a scan, or justify
extrapolating an empty-pack population. No new measurement was made in the
design correction. Prior reported figures are not acceptance evidence.

## Actions

- Inspect the native format and reader for an authoritative complete-content
  indicator. If unavailable, use bounded streaming inspection of all relevant
  text content, with yielding/cancellation; do not read whole packs into RAM.
- Define and document which native text fields establish presence, and test
  complete-content semantics. Empty means verified absence of text, not a
  sparse-content threshold. A partial sample or read failure is unknown.
- Introduce the verified-empty classification outside indexed coverage, with
  a non-repeating scheduling treatment. Preserve freshness/identity checks:
  source or processor changes must invalidate an earlier empty observation.
- Propagate the classification through the cache-hit path, coverage counters,
  census snapshots and 0744's view. A generic cache hit must not restore
  `current` for a previously verified empty pack.
- Commit the probe and evidence in verification/ before claiming the reader
  mechanism has been established. Reference them here. No source-layer or OCR
  diagnosis follows from empty native content alone.

## Verification

- [ ] A well-formed empty native pack differs from indexed text.
- [ ] Sparse nonempty text and text appearing only late in a document remain
      nonempty; partial reads and corrupt/unreadable content are not empty.
- [ ] A cache hit preserves the verified-empty result; source and processor
      changes invalidate it and permit normal reinspection/re-extraction.
- [ ] Empty packs do not create a repeated extraction loop.
- [ ] Coverage counts and 0744's data view agree after incremental updates
      and completed reconciliation.
- [ ] Content inspection remains bounded, yielding and cancellable.
- [ ] Reader-contract evidence is committed and referenced here.
- [ ] `make check` passes.

## Exit criteria

Verified empty native content is distinguished from searchable text throughout
inspection, caching, scheduling and reporting under SPEC.md §5.2.7. No native
extraction settings, source files or extraction implementation are changed.
